  "headline": "The unit command controller is a ten-slot command queue at +54h (stride 1Ch) plus a one-slot override at +188h. A command is a pointer to one of the 26 eight-byte singletons in 00E08EF8..00E08FC7; the per-command data is a separate 18h-byte parameter record stored at slot+4h. The command classes carry no behaviour: every class vtable is five constant getters (six for moveto and moveonpath), so there is no per-class begin/step/end. All execution is in the controller, which dispatches by comparing the command pointer against the singleton addresses.",
